## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop:** `Game` class holds all state; `SeededRandom` (`this.rng.next()`) used in genMap/genPeople/fireEvent/spawnCaravan; `endTurn()` runs numbered steps 1-9 in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map:** `genMap()` builds 8x8 grid from seed; `canBuild()` checks `tile.terrain !== building.terrain`. Adjacency (`config.adjacency`, `has_adj`) only used in `showTileTooltip()` text, never multiplies actual production in `endTurn()`. Score 1.

**F3 — Economy:** Greenhouse consumes `requirements.water` to produce `food` (real 1-step chain), caps/overflow enforced. But `FORGE` requires ore+power yet has empty `production: []` — metal is never produced by anything, breaking the intended ore→metal chain. Score 1.

**F4 — Population:** `people[]` records with skill/fatigue/morale/job; `worker.skill`, `worker.fatigue`, `worker.morale` read in `endTurn()` production loop to set `output_mult`. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs:** `food_shortage`/`water_shortage` computed each turn; writes `p.morale -= 10*(...)`; `worker.morale < 50` reduces `output_mult`; recovery via events/`morale-focus` research, not instant. Score 2.

**F6 — Research:** 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; `queueResearch()` enforces prereqs/costs. Effects mostly hardcoded checks (`research_done['better-farming']` etc.) work, but `water-retention` (`water_cap_mult`) and `ore-refining` (`ore_to_metal_mult`) effect objects are never read anywhere — 2 of 8 nodes are dead. Score 1.

**F7 — Events:** 10 entries in `event_list`, all with 2 choices with differing `action()` state changes; `events_cooldown[event.name]=turn+10` enforced. But selection is `Math.floor(rng.next()*available.length)` — uniform, not weighted. Score 1.

**F8 — Trade:** `caravan_prices` computed from `this.resources[item]/storage_caps[item]` plus rng jitter; `caravan_inventory` limited and decremented; `tradeWith()` implements both buy/sell branches. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard:** `turn % 8 === 0` triggers storm, `storm_severity` grows every turn and scales damage; `storm-shelter` research reduces `storm_dmg`; repair spends `parts` and restores `health`. But production loop's `output_mult` never reads `building.health` — damaged buildings produce at full rate. Score 1.

**F10 — Save/load:** `serializeState()`/`hashState()` exist only for internal test/benchmark use; no export-to-text UI, no paste/import parser anywhere. Score 0.

**F11 — End conditions:** win check `turn>=60 && people.length>=12` and lose check `people.length===0` both in `endTurn()`; `endGame()` computes `score` from pop/research/resources/turn and renders `endGameModal`. Score 2.

**F12 — UI:** `switchTab()` wired to tab buttons and keydown Digit1-5; log entries show `T${entry.turn}:`; `showTileTooltip()` explains costs/bonuses; `@media (max-width:600px)` adapts layout. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel:** `devRunTests()` has real invariant checks (health 0-100, skill 1-5, fatigue 0-100, prereq consistency, hash roundtrip) mixed with a couple of trivial ones. `devBenchmark()` runs 200 `sim.endTurn()` calls and prints `hashState()`, but `sim.newGame()`/`sim.updateUI()` writes to the *same* DOM ids as the live game (`mapGrid`, `stats`, etc.), so it is not actually headless/without-UI. Score 1.

**G1 — research → yield:** `research_done['better-farming']` etc. read directly inside the `endTurn()` production formula (`amount *= 1.2`), hardcoded per-id special case rather than generic effect application. Score 2.

**G2 — shortfall → morale → output:** `food_shortage`/`water_shortage` → `p.morale -= 10*(1-p.morale/100)` → `worker.morale < 50` triggers `output_mult *= 0.7` in same `endTurn()`. Binary threshold rather than continuous curve. Score 3.

**G3 — storm → damage → output → repair:** `buildings[idx].health` reduced by storm; repair spends `parts` and restores `health`; but production `output_mult` never references `health`, so damage never reduces output. Score 1.

**G4 — trade prices ↔ stockpiles:** `caravan_prices[item]` computed from `supply_mod = 1 + (resources[item]/storage_caps[item])*0.5`, recalculated each caravan spawn (every 15 turns). Score 3.

**G5 — event choices mutate state:** `Settler Arrival` choice pushes to `this.people` and deducts `resources.food`; `Morale Boost` choice deducts food and raises all `p.morale`; both durable, applied via `choice.action()` on click. Score 4.

